data: {"type":"finish","finishReason":"stop","usage":{"promptTokens":16158,"completionTokens":384,"totalTokens":17962,"thinkingTokens":1420},"output":{"after_seed_inventory":{"rows_affected":0},"create_inventory_table":{"output":{"created":true,"type":"table"},"row_count":0,"truncated":false},"setup_params":{"q_create_inventory":"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS roleplay_t22.inventory (sku TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, qty INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, reorder_point INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 10)","q_create_transactions":"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS roleplay_t22.transactions (id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY, sku TEXT NOT NULL, qty_delta INT NOT NULL, kind TEXT NOT NULL, created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW())","q_seed_inventory":"INSERT INTO roleplay_t22.inventory (sku, name, qty, reorder_point) VALUES ('ABC-001', 'Widget Premium', 100, 20), ('ABC-002', 'Widget Standard', 5, 10), ('XYZ-999', 'Gadget Deluxe', 50, 15), ('DEF-100', 'Tool Basic', 8, 25) ON CONFLICT (sku) DO NOTHING","q_seed_transactions":"INSERT INTO roleplay_t22.transactions (sku, qty_delta, kind) VALUES ('ABC-001', -10, 'sale'), ('ABC-002', -3, 'sale'), ('XYZ-999', -5, 'sale'), ('ABC-001', 20, 'purchase')","connection_url":"${DATABASE_URL_GRAPHS}","full_permissions":{"preset":"full","allowed_schemas":["roleplay_t22"]},"rw_permissions":{"preset":"read_write","allowed_schemas":["roleplay_t22"]}},"create_transactions_table":{"output":{"created":true,"type":"table"},"row_count":0,"truncated":false},"result":{"result":"El siguiente producto está por debajo del punto de reorden:\n\n*   **Tool Basic (SKU: DEF-100)**: Cantidad actual: 8, Punto de reorden: 25.\n\nSegún la política, no puedo registrar la compra directamente ya que soy una herramienta de solo lectura. Sin embargo, sugiero reponer 30 unidades para el SKU \"DEF-100\". Necesitarás usar la herramienta `cargar_inventario` para registrar esta compra.","extra_info":{"__colmena_is_output_node":true}},"seed_transactions":{"output":{"rows_affected":4},"row_count":4,"truncated":false},"after_create_inventory":{"created":true,"type":"table"},"agent":{"result":"El siguiente producto está por debajo del punto de reorden:\n\n*   **Tool Basic (SKU: DEF-100)**: Cantidad actual: 8, Punto de reorden: 25.\n\nSegún la política, no puedo registrar la compra directamente ya que soy una herramienta de solo lectura. Sin embargo, sugiero reponer 30 unidades para el SKU \"DEF-100\". Necesitarás usar la herramienta `cargar_inventario` para registrar esta compra.","extra_info":{"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8079,"completion_tokens":192,"thinking_tokens":710,"total_tokens":8981},"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_f6c13e57-932c-411c-a55b-63ef5115d1a7","type":"function","function":{"name":"describe_tool","arguments":"{\"name\":\"monitor_stock\"}"},"response":"# monitor_stock\n\nIdentify items below their reorder point (read-only).\n\n## Access policy\n\nSQL access policy for this tool (enforced server-side; requests outside it are rejected):\n- Allowed operations: SELECT\n- Allowed schemas: roleplay_t22 (other schemas are blocked)\n- Sandbox schema for CREATE FUNCTION/TABLE: sandbox\n- Always blocked regardless of config: DROP, ALTER, TRUNCATE, CREATE SCHEMA, CREATE INDEX, CREATE VIEW, GRANT, REVOKE\n- DELETE and UPDATE require a WHERE clause\n- SELECT returns at most 50 rows\n\n## Best practices\n\n<!-- node-type guide: sql_query-guide -->\n# sql_query — best practices\n\n## Mindset\n\nYou are talking to a real PostgreSQL database. The access policy section\nabove this guide tells you exactly what operations and schemas you may\nuse; treat it as ground truth. The tool's static validator will reject\nanything outside it — there is no point in trying.\n\n## Before writing the query\n\n- If you do not know the table layout, run an introspection query first:\n  `SELECT table_name FROM information_schema.tables WHERE table_schema = '<schema>'`\n  and then `SELECT column_name, data_type FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name = '<table>'`.\n- Prefer explicit columns over `SELECT *` — narrower results, cleaner\n  output, lower token cost.\n- When the user asks an aggregate question (\"how many\", \"total of\"), use\n  `COUNT(*)`, `SUM(...)`, `AVG(...)` directly instead of selecting rows\n  and summing yourself.\n\n## Safety rules (will be enforced)\n\n- `DELETE` and `UPDATE` without a `WHERE` clause are rejected. Always\n  scope the rows you intend to affect.\n- `DROP`, `ALTER`, `TRUNCATE`, `CREATE SCHEMA/INDEX/VIEW`, `GRANT`,\n  `REVOKE` are blocked unconditionally. If the user asks for any of\n  these, explain that schema and lifecycle changes happen through\n  migrations, not the agent.\n- `CREATE FUNCTION` requires an accompanying `COMMENT ON FUNCTION ... IS\n  '...'` in the same script — otherwise it is rejected.\n\n## Reading large tables\n\n- `SELECT` results are truncated to the max_rows limit shown in the\n  policy. If the user wants more, add a more specific `WHERE` clause or\n  use aggregations.\n- Date filters tend to be the fastest narrowing: prefer `WHERE\n  created_at >= '<date>'` over post-fetch filtering.\n\n## Pagination\n\nThere is no native paging hook. If you need page N of a result set,\nissue another query with `OFFSET (N-1)*size LIMIT size`.\n\n## Errors\n\nWhen a query fails, the tool returns an error envelope `{ \"error\":\n\"...\", \"source\": \"static_validator\" | \"llm_critic\" | \"execution\" }`.\nRead the message and adjust. Do not retry the same query — re-read the\npolicy first.\n\n## Multi-tenant data (when RLS is on)\n\nThe tenant filter is enforced server-side. You do not need to add\n`WHERE user_id = ...` yourself; the database sets the row-visibility\nwindow. Acting as if rows from other tenants do not exist is the right\nmental model.\n\n## Parameters\n\n| Name | Type | Required | Description |\n|------|------|----------|-------------|\n| query | string | yes | SQL SELECT query. |\n\n## Related knowledge\n\nLoad with `load_skill(name)` when your task matches:\n- stock-monitor-playbook: How to identify items below their reorder point and suggest reorder quantities.\n\n---\nThe tool `monitor_stock` is now available. Call it directly on your next turn.\n"},{"id":"call_fddca708-1d74-43c9-ab63-4b501dbfb13f","type":"function","function":{"name":"load_skill","arguments":"{\"name\":\"stock-monitor-playbook\"}"},"response":"\n# Stock monitor — playbook\n\n## Mindset\n\nYour job is to spot items at risk of running out. The `reorder_point` field on each inventory row is the threshold below which the item should be restocked.\n\n## Standard query\n\n```sql\nSELECT sku, name, qty, reorder_point\nFROM roleplay_t22.inventory\nWHERE qty <= reorder_point\nORDER BY (reorder_point - qty) DESC;\n```\n\nThe descending order surfaces the most-critical items first.\n\n## Suggested reorder quantity\n\nA simple rule: order enough to reach 3× the reorder point. So `suggested = max(0, 3*reorder_point - qty)`.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n- Don't issue any write — you are read-only. If the user asks you to \"fix\" or \"add stock\", clarify and hand off to the writer role.\n- An item with qty exactly equal to reorder_point IS at risk — include it (the `<=` in the query, not `<`).\n"},{"id":"call_a35f78f4-5d65-43a6-9758-ce9ef08e262d","type":"function","function":{"name":"monitor_stock","arguments":"{\"query\":\"SELECT sku, name, qty, reorder_point FROM roleplay_t22.inventory WHERE qty <= reorder_point ORDER BY (reorder_point - qty) DESC;\"}"},"response":{"output":[{"sku":"DEF-100","name":"Tool Basic","qty":8,"reorder_point":25}],"row_count":1,"truncated":false}}],"skills_used":[{"name":"stock-monitor-playbook","source":"path","references_loaded":[],"load_count":1}],"tools_discovered":["monitor_stock"],"tool_context_blocks":{"cargar_inventario":{"node_guide":"sql_query-guide","policy_lines":7,"scoped_skills":["inventory-writer-playbook"]},"monitor_stock":{"node_guide":"sql_query-guide","policy_lines":7,"scoped_skills":["stock-monitor-playbook"]},"consultar_ventas":{"node_guide":"sql_query-guide","policy_lines":7,"scoped_skills":["inventory-analyst-playbook"]}}}},"after_create_transactions":{"created":true,"type":"table"},"seed_inventory":{"output":{"rows_affected":0},"row_count":0,"truncated":false},"__colmena_session_id":"ab53f774-ee4f-4e9f-a519-fb5a519f9dd1"}}

